/Title (Recent industry developments underscore this shift: many national firms are consolidating under single brands, centralizing middle- and back-office functions, and reorienting toward corporate operating structures to drive private-equity returns. These changes may make sense for aging owners seeking a graceful exit, but they can stifle innovation and limit the flexibility of growth-oriented advisors.)
